# This repository is built and run on Linux. A CRLF that reaches the image
# is not cosmetic: a shell script whose shebang ends in \r makes the kernel
# look for an interpreter whose name ends in \r, and the add-on dies at
# startup with "unable to exec bashio". Normalise on the way in, check out
# LF everywhere, whatever the developer's platform does.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
